## TEACHER DASHBOARD

---
NOTE: The Material Section, Exam Section, and Assignment Section are all tied to the Subject Management system
configured by the Admin. This means that when a teacher creates and publishes an assignment, material,
or exam, the content must be targeted to a specific class — and only students who belong to that class
code will be able to see and access it.

To support this, whenever a teacher publishes or submits content in any of these three sections, the
system must present the teacher with two scoped selection steps before publishing:

1. **Select Subject** — A dropdown showing only the subjects assigned to that teacher (as configured
   by the Admin via the Subject Management panel).
2. **Select Class** — Based on the selected subject, a second dropdown shows the class code(s) linked
   to that subject.

This two-step selection ensures that content is always delivered to the correct class. For example, if
a teacher handles "Mathematics" for class 1A and "Physics" for class 2B, publishing a Mathematics
assignment will only make it visible to students in class 1A — students in class 2B will never see it.

On the student side, the system must filter all incoming assignments, materials, and exams by matching
the student's class code against the class code selected by the teacher at the time of publishing. Only
content where the class codes match should be returned and displayed to the student.
---

### Material Section
- [x] Display list of materials created by the logged-in teacher (scoped by `teacherId`)
- [x] Implement **Create Material** form:
  - Text input box (rich text or plain textarea)
  - Multi-file upload input (accept multiple files; store as array of file references)
- [x] Implement **Edit Material** — update text and/or replace/add/remove files
- [x] Implement **Delete Material** — with confirmation modal; also delete associated files from storage

### Assignment Section
- [x] Display list of assignments created by the logged-in teacher
- [x] Implement **Create Assignment** form:
  - Text input (instructions)
  - Multi-file upload
- [x] Implement **Edit Assignment**
- [x] Implement **Delete Assignment** — delete assignment files AND any student submissions associated with itssions or mark them as orphaned

### Exam Section
- [ ] Display list of exam forms created by the logged-in teacher with status badge: `draft` | `published`
- [ ] Implement **Exam Form Builder** (modeled after Google Forms):
  - Add question blocks dynamically
  - Each question block supports the following types (all optional, rendered in this fixed order):
    1. **Multiple Choice** — input for question text + add/remove answer options + mark correct answer
    2. **Essay** — input for question prompt (free-text answer by student)
    3. **File Upload** — input for question prompt (file submission by student)
  - Allow reordering of question blocks via drag-and-drop or up/down controls
  - Set **total questions created** and **random display count** (randomCount must be ≤ totalQuestions; enforce validation)
- [ ] Implement **Save (Draft)** — saves exam to DB with `status: 'draft'`; NOT visible to students
- [ ] Implement **Publish** — updates exam `status` to `'published'`; becomes visible to students
- [ ] Implement **Unpublish** — revert `status` back to `'draft'` if needed
- [ ] Implement **Edit Exam Form** — edit questions, options, and randomization settings (only if status is `draft`)
- [ ] Implement **Delete Exam Form** — with confirmation; also clean up related `examSessions`

