## STUDENT DASHBOARD

### Assignment Section
- [ ] Display list of assignments from the student's linked subject(s) and class
- [ ] For each assignment, show submission status: `not submitted` | `submitted`
- [ ] Implement **Submit Assignment**:
  - Text input box (student's answer/response)
  - Multi-file upload input
  - Save as a `submission` document linked to `assignmentId` and `studentId`
- [ ] Implement **Edit Submission** — update text and/or files (only before deadline if deadline logic is added)
- [ ] Implement **Delete Submission** — with confirmation

### Material Section
- [ ] Display list of materials linked to the student's subject(s) and class
- [ ] Show material text content and list of attached files
- [ ] Each file has a **Download** button — trigger file download from storage URL
- [ ] Students have NO create, edit, or delete access in this section

### Exam Section

#### Pre-Exam: Notification Permission Gate
- [ ] Before a student can enter any exam tab/page, show a **Notification Permission Modal**:
  - Prompt: "You must enable browser notifications to take this exam."
  - Call `Notification.requestPermission()` from the browser API
  - If permission is **denied** → block access to the exam; show a message asking them to enable notifications in browser settings
  - If permission is **granted** → allow entry and store permission state in session

#### Exam Session & Tab-Exit Detection
- [ ] When student starts an exam, create an `examSession` document:
  ```
  { examId, studentId, exitCount: 0, startedAt, status: 'in-progress' }
  ```
- [ ] Implement **tab visibility detection** using the `document.visibilitychange` event:
  - Start a timer when `document.hidden === true`
  - If the student remains outside the tab for **≥ 15 seconds**:
    - Increment `exitCount` in the `examSession` document (server-side PATCH request)
    - Send a browser push notification: *"Warning: You left the exam tab. [X] violation(s) recorded."*
  - If the student returns within 15 seconds, cancel the timer — do NOT increment `exitCount`
- [ ] Lockout rule:
  - If `exitCount >= 2` → set session `status: 'locked'`
  - Redirect student to a lockout page: *"You have been removed from this exam session due to multiple tab exits. Please contact your teacher."*
  - Locked sessions cannot be resumed; a teacher must reset or create a new session if applicable
- [ ] Implement **Answer Submission**:
  - Collect answers for all displayed questions (multiple choice selection, essay text, uploaded files)
  - On submit, save answers to the `examSession` document and set `status: 'submitted'`

#### Exam Question Randomization (enforce server-side)
- [ ] On exam start, server fetches the exam's full question list and `randomCount`
- [ ] Server randomly selects `randomCount` questions from the full list using a shuffle algorithm (e.g. Fisher-Yates)
- [ ] Return only the selected and shuffled questions to the client
- [ ] Each student session gets its own randomized set — do NOT reuse the same order across sessions

---

## MANDATORY — Data Synchronization Rules

- [ ] All assignments, materials, and exams must be scoped by `subjectId`
- [ ] `subjectId` links to a `{ teacherId, subjectName, classCode }` document
- [ ] When a subject is updated or deleted by Admin, cascade the change to all referencing documents or mark them as unlinked
- [ ] Students only see content (assignments, materials, exams) that belongs to their class code
- [ ] Teachers only see and manage content they created (filter by `teacherId`)
- [ ] Apply server-side RBAC middleware on every API route — reject requests where the session role does not match the required role for that route
```